Subject: Cantor Identity Accounting Store Bootstrap P3 Solution

@ [solution_uuid] d4d465db-1883-4805-86c7-4fc173c95f8f

& [ImplementedSolution]
  + BootstrapStoreConfig binds the ledger file explicit journal identity target directory and all capacity limits
  + bootstrap_identity_accounting_store validates canonical P0 input builds P1 genesis creates an absent target persists and reloads through P2 and returns BootstrapReceipt
  + cantor-identity-accounting-bootstrap provides the exact one-shot command surface and canonical receipt stdout

& [SafetyShape]
  + the ledger is fully admitted before target creation success follows reload pre-existing paths are never removed and cleanup uses remove_dir rather than recursive deletion

& [Boundary] is a machine-form custody transition, not a semantic object-authoring or Judgment mechanism
